# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored — never commit a real token.
#
# API token used by `npm run devlink:export`.
# The CLI asks for a Workspace API token: Webflow Dashboard → Apps & Integrations
# → Manage → Workspace API Token. A Site API token with component + asset read
# access also works for DevLink export; if one fails, try the other.
#
# Only needed locally to pull components. The Webflow Cloud build does not need
# it, because the generated `src/devlink/` output is committed to the repo.
WEBFLOW_API_TOKEN=

# Optional. The site is already pinned as `siteId` in webflow.json
# (6a73c4d12df78ea4c276a06b — the "Stone" site). Setting this overrides it.
# WEBFLOW_SITE_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Agentbox --
# Reapit Sales (Agentbox) API credentials. Used only by
# `npm run agentbox:probe`, which fetches one listing so the field mapping in
# src/lib/ingestion/agentbox-mapping.ts can be checked against reality.
#
# The probe reads these from the environment or from `.dev.vars`. Both are
# gitignored. In Webflow Cloud they are environment variables of type Secret,
# set per environment.
#
# AGENTBOX_CLIENT_ID is base64 of the Agentbox admin URL, and it is what
# selects the instance. The client refuses one that does not decode to a
# sandbox unless asked to allow production explicitly.
AGENTBOX_CLIENT_ID=
AGENTBOX_API_KEY=

# Put the real values in `.dev.vars`, not here — this file is committed.
#
# Sandbox is the default, and the scripts refuse a client ID that does not
# decode to one. When the production credentials arrive, opt in per-run with
# `--allow-production`, or set this in a shell that only holds live keys.
# AGENTBOX_ALLOW_PRODUCTION=true
